## 14. Development Tools

| Tool | Purpose | Used In MOT |
|---|---|---|
| **STM32CubeIDE** | Eclipse-based IDE: edit, build, debug | Primary IDE |
| **STM32CubeMX** | GUI tool to configure pins, clocks, peripherals → generates C init code | `.ioc` file |
| **ARM GCC** | Cross-compiler (`arm-none-eabi-gcc`) | Build toolchain |
| **ST-Link** | JTAG/SWD debug probe (built into Nucleo/Discovery boards) | Flash & debug |
| **OpenOCD** | Open-source debug server (alternative to ST-Link utilities) | CLI flashing |
| **STM32CubeProgrammer** | ST's standalone flash programming tool | Alternative flasher |

### 14.1 Build Process

```
Source files (.c, .s)
        │
        ▼
ARM GCC Compiler → Object files (.o)
        │
        ▼
ARM GCC Linker + STM32F407VGTX_FLASH.ld → OT_RTOS.elf
        │
        ▼
objcopy → OT_RTOS.bin (optional, for OTA)
```

### 14.2 Debugging with SWD

```
PC (STM32CubeIDE / OpenOCD)
        │
    USB cable
        │
        ▼
    ST-Link probe
        │
    SWD (2 wires: SWDIO + SWCLK)
        │
        ▼
    STM32F407VGTx (target)
```

**SWD (Serial Wire Debug)** uses only 2 wires instead of JTAG's 5, providing:
- Flash programming
- Breakpoints (6 hardware breakpoints in Cortex-M4)
- Memory/register inspection
- Real-time variable watching (SWV)

